secb.scenario:
Chai Nagri Foods (CNF), a Rawalpindi-based tea company, has launched a new ready-to-drink 'Kashmiri chai' product. During the first month of the launch CNF's marketing team tracked the product's hashtag and every mention of the brand on Facebook, Instagram and X, and produced a daily sentiment score.
The sentiment score showed 82% positive comments. However, sales in the first month were only 40% of target. A review of the data found that:
(i) many 'positive' comments, written in Roman Urdu, were actually sarcastic (for example, 'Wah, itni meethi chai, dentist khush ho jayega');
(ii) a large number of glowing posts came from influencers paid by CNF, without disclosing the payment;
(iii) several hundred comments came from newly created accounts posting identical text within minutes of each other;
(iv) popular posts were re-shared thousands of times and each share was counted as a separate opinion.

